msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:42
msgid "Track AI crawler visits on this site"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:47
msgid "Store the page path for each visit (per-page breakdowns)"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:49
msgid "Turn this off to keep only one aggregate row per crawler per day."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:52
msgid "Keep crawler logs for"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:54
msgid "30 days"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:55
msgid "90 days"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:56
msgid "180 days"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:62
msgid "Send daily crawler totals to my Rezolve Ai project"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:65
msgid "Optional. When enabled, Rezolve Ai receives one aggregate row per crawler per day (crawler name, date, hit count). No IP addresses, cookies, or personal information ever leave your site. This setting covers crawlers only; visitor pageviews are a separate setting below and are off unless you turn them on."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:68
msgid "Tracking, path storage, and retention all run entirely on this site and are active right now. Only the optional daily report, which sends totals to Rezolve Ai, needs an account."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:74
msgid "Visitor pageviews"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:75
msgid "Counts how many times each published page was viewed, so Rezolve Ai can show what your content changes did to real traffic."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:79
msgid "Count visitor pageviews on this site"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:82
msgid "Adds a small script to published pages that records one count per view. It stores no cookie, no session, and no IP address, so it cannot tell one visitor from another and reports pageviews rather than visitors. Logged-in editors and administrators are never counted, and neither are crawlers."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:85
msgid "A script is used rather than server-side counting because page caching serves most visitors without WordPress ever running, which would undercount heavily."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:90
msgid "Send daily pageview and sales totals to my Rezolve Ai project"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:93
msgid "Optional, and separate from the crawler setting above. Rezolve Ai receives one row per page per day (page, date, view count, and the referring site for visits from search and AI assistants), and for WooCommerce stores one row per product per day (units and revenue). No order details, customer records, names, email addresses or postal addresses are ever sent."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:96
msgid "Counting works on its own with no account. Only the daily report needs one."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:102
msgid "A/B test your product copy"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:103
msgid "Shows different versions of a product description to different visitors and measures which one sells better. Experiments are set up in Rezolve Ai; this switch decides whether this site takes part."
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:107
msgid "Split visitors between versions on this site"
msgstr ""

#: admin/views/page-settings.php:110
msgid "This is the one feature here that stores a cookie. To remember which version a visitor saw, it keeps a random id in their browser. Nothing happens without their consent: it uses the WordPress Consent API, so your cookie banner decides. If you have no consent plugin, nothing is stored and every visitor sees your normal copy."
